<!--Post: 970--><!--Time: 1094170490-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST970"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Micaela<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Micaela<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, September 02, 2004 - 5:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think BTK was/is a Wichita Beat/Vortex wanna be. He seemed to be very influenced by William Burroughs. William Burroughs, famous poet, killer &#40;of his wife&#41;, writer and Kansas Beat/Vortex member was closely linked to PJ Harvey. He did music, poetry reading and even a short movie with her. She is one messed up individual! Any ideas?  <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.askmen.com/women/singer_100/103_pj_harvey.html" target=_top>http://www.askmen.com/women/singer_100/103_pj_harv ey.html</a> <BR> <BR><a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PJ_Harvey" target=_top>http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PJ_Harvey</a> <BR> <BR><a href="http://acidkiss.com/dry/modules.php?name=book&amp;file=cast" target=_top>http://acidkiss.com/dry/modules.php?name=book&amp;file =cast</a> <BR> <BR><a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Book_of_Life" target=_top>http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Book_of_Life</a> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 970-->
<!--Post: 1045--><!--Time: 1095515331-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1045"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, September 18, 2004 - 6:48 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This PJ does appear to be one sick puppy. Since BTK does like inversions and mirror images, etc., could he be pulling a fast one and actually be referring to some letters surrounding the P and J in the alphabet? Just a thought. He does love to send everyone on a wild goose chase. KO would be a couple of those letters: boxing perhaps? <BR> <BR>If he follows the discussion groups, I&#39;m sure that he is amused by all the speculations and loves all this attention. I would not be surprised at all to find that within his various communications he has embedded his name and some other identifying info. He loves to do a little sidestep and lead the people on.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1045-->
<!--Post: 1049--><!--Time: 1095799507-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1049"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, September 21, 2004 - 1:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It&#39;s definitely a possibility.  However, WPD isn&#39;t helping matters any by withholding as much information as they can.  They&#39;re not rocket scientists, and the answer is probably right under their collective nose.  If they had let the public in on a lot of what they do know since Day One &#40;ie, BTK&#39;s letters, among other things&#41;, the case might have been solved 3 decades ago.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1049-->
<!--Post: 1052--><!--Time: 1095828618-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1052"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, September 21, 2004 - 9:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There is a character in the movie “Carrie” by the name of Norma Watson. Her real name is “P.J. Soles.” <BR>The movie falls within the timeline of Dr. P.J. Wyatt’s classes. <BR>“Reviews of university archives of course catalogs show that from 1964 -- when she began teaching at the university -- until spring of 1977, Wyatt taught the course nine times.”  <BR><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/9458681.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/9458681.htm</a> <BR> <BR>Carrie <BR><a href="http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0074285/" target=_top>http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0074285/</a> <BR>“In Theatres: 03 November, 1976”  <BR><a href="http://www.movieusher.com/ProductDetail.aspx?asin=6304508611" target=_top>http://www.movieusher.com/ProductDetail.aspx?asin= 6304508611</a> <BR> <BR>In the movie “Carrie” there is a scene where they kill a pig. <BR>“Curly Locks! Curly Locks! wilt thou be mine? <BR>Thou shalt not wash the dishes, nor yet feed the swine,” <BR><a href="http://www.ongoing-tales.com/SERIALS/oldtime/POETRY/curlylocks.html" target=_top>http://www.ongoing-tales.com/SERIALS/oldtime/POETR Y/curlylocks.html</a> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1052-->
<!--Post: 1120--><!--Time: 1097210588-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1120"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, October 07, 2004 - 9:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->P.J. Scout is a search vehicle listing jobs at the Law Company, Nancy Fox&#39;s employer.  This is all too wierd.  This may not be relevant to BTK&#39;s PJ of so many years ago, but just another case of coincidence. Wasn&#39;t Vicki Wegerle&#39;s church undergoing some renovations at the time of her death? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
